cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hypnos, please cite it AND the original source of each model record you use."
title: "Hypnos: a curated, tier-annotated dataset of anesthetic PK/PD models"
abstract: >-
  Hypnos is a curated, citation-backed, machine-readable dataset of the
  population pharmacokinetic-pharmacodynamic models that anesthetic simulation,
  TCI research, and depth-of-anesthesia modeling depend on. Every model carries
  an explicit confidence tier, its derivation population, its applicability
  envelope, its documented failure modes, and its published predictive-
  performance metrics, and exports into PharmML, NONMEM, nlmixr2/rxode2, Pumas,
  and SBML. It is not a dosing tool and not a pump driver; it is the honest,
  reusable ground-truth layer beneath them.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Good
    given-names: Clay
version: 0.7.0
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/clay-good/hypnos/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clay-good/hypnos"
keywords:
  - pharmacokinetics
  - pharmacodynamics
  - anesthesia
  - propofol
  - target-controlled infusion
  - pharmacometrics
